  "classification": {
    "positioning": {
      "title": "Strategic Genre Positioning",
      "subtitle": "A reflective historical mystery pulsing with modern identity conflicts and royal intrigue",
      "description": "The Broken Crown occupies a unique niche at the intersection of historical fiction, suspense, and introspective literary drama. By embedding royal secrets within a contemporary European setting, it delivers a modern treasure hunt wrapped inside intergenerational trauma and unresolved grief. Its market positioning leverages rich emotional introspection and intellectual intrigue that appeals to an upmarket commercial readership. Anchoring its narrative to historically grounded material while exploring current themes such as institutional failure and moral ambiguity, it distinguishes itself from faster-paced thrillers and instead caters to readers seeking depth, character development, and historical resonance."
    },
    "moodAndTone": {
      "title": "Mood and Tonal Landscape",
      "subtitle": "A quietly gripping tale steeped in reflection, tension, and secrecy",
      "description": "The Broken Crown crafts a predominantly introspective and suspenseful mood, balancing reflective narration with isolated moments of intensity and conflict. Emotions of curiosity, nostalgia, apprehension, and moral ambiguity recur, evoking a meditative yet mysterious tone reminiscent of European literary noir. Subtle emotional waxing and waning align the reader with the protagonist’s psychological and relational struggles, while historical insertion and vivid descriptive framing contribute a contemplative, often claustrophobic atmospheric richness. The tension is psychological and structural rather than sensational, enabling deeper immersion into emotional and historical complexities."
    },
